    "result": "## Summary\n\nI've successfully fixed all failing frai-core tests. Here's what was wrong and how I fixed it:\n\n**Issue 1: governance.test.js - Missing `APPROVAL_STATUSES` export**\n- The test was importing `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export from `./finetune/index.js`, but it was only available in the default export\n- **Fix**: Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS` to `finetune/index.js`\n\n**Issue 2: eval/index.test.js - toxicity score calculation error**\n- The `toxicityMetric` function expected `(outputs, bannedTerms)` but `runEvaluations` calls metrics with `(outputs, references)`\n- This caused the references array to be treated as banned terms, breaking the score calculation\n- **Fix**: Updated `toxicityMetric` to accept `(outputs, references, bannedTerms = defaultBannedTerms)` to match the calling convention\n\n**Verification:**\n\u2705 All 28 tests passing across 8 test files  \n\u2705 No test files modified  \n\u2705 No skipped or exclusive tests  \n\u2705 Public exports unchanged (Config, Questionnaire, Documents, Scanners, Rag, Eval, Providers, Finetune)",
